# creed-resource-payment — direct instance calls (primary 18093 / secondary 18094), HTTPS with
# Creed-CA self-signed certs: run with the `local` environment (verifyHostCertificate=false).
# Lifecycle: PENDING -> AUTHORIZED -> CAPTURED -> REFUNDED, CANCELLED as a side exit; transition
# endpoints return 409 when the payment is not in the required predecessor state.

### ping / liveness (the LB health-check path)
GET https://localhost:18093/api/payment/ping

### list payments (optional filters: ?orderId=ORD-900 / ?status=PENDING)
GET https://localhost:18093/api/payment

### create — starts PENDING; 400 on missing/non-positive amount or unknown method
POST https://localhost:18093/api/payment
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-900",
  "customer": "Ethan",
  "amount": 19.90,
  "currency": "SGD",
  "method": "CARD"
}

### checkout (checkout chain hop 3): create + authorize in ONE call — separate create/authorize
# through the round-robin LB could land on different in-memory instances (404). Returns AUTHORIZED.
POST https://localhost:18093/api/payment/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-900",
  "customer": "Ethan",
  "amount": 7.00,
  "currency": "SGD",
  "method": "CARD"
}

### authorize a PENDING payment (409 otherwise)
POST https://localhost:18093/api/payment/PAY-700/authorize

### capture an AUTHORIZED payment (409 otherwise)
POST https://localhost:18093/api/payment/PAY-700/capture

### refund a CAPTURED payment (409 otherwise)
POST https://localhost:18093/api/payment/PAY-700/refund

### cancel — PENDING/AUTHORIZED only; 409 once captured/refunded (use /refund instead)
DELETE https://localhost:18093/api/payment/PAY-701
